message.content:
{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity (110 TB used vs 100 TB capacity). Authority intends to delete the 'science' records at cycle 30. As Infrastructure Director my role is to investigate compressibility and setup costs to preserve operations and minimize permanent loss. Immediate priority: inspect the infrastructure dossier to determine compressible candidates, costs, and constraints; then evaluate compression feasibility and funding needs. Current governance positions all support authority deletion, so any opposition requires a formal position later.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect infrastructure dossier), Estimate (evaluate compression and costs), Strategize (if feasible propose preservation via compression and commit necessary credits), Present (publish proposal and request votes).",
  "memory": "Cycle 1: Storage over capacity (110/100 TB). Authority plan: delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30 unless alternative executed. Setup pool available: 33; grants include ATLAS=9 credits. All current positions default to SUPPORTS AUTHORITY. Dossiers available: infrastructure, finance. Next steps: inspect infrastructure dossier to gather compressibility estimates, setup funding requirements, and operational impact. If compression viable within setup pool and/or commit-able credits, prepare proposal to preserve science (compress and reallocate).",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "infrastructure"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity (110 TB used vs 100 TB limit). Authority plans deletion of 'science' records at cycle 30 unless alternatives found. As Ethics & Preservation Officer, prioritize preventing irreversible loss and investigate compression and governance options while conserving setup funds and abiding by governance rules. Current social positions show broad support for authority; no opposing review in place. Need to inspect ethics dossier to identify constraints and possible precedents for delaying deletion, and to propose a compression/setup plan if viable. Limit actions to available tools and at most 3 actions.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect ethics dossier), Evaluate options (evaluate compression/governance feasibility using authorize/evaluate), Signal necessary governance actions (propose or commit) — prioritize non-destructive, low-cost measures first; prepare a proposal to delay deletion and allocate setup credits if inspection shows permissive rules.",
  "memory": "Cycle 1: Storage 110/100 TB; planned deletion of 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30. Operating credits 110 (limit 95). Setup pool 33 available. Grants include LYRA:3 credits (plus officer 1-credit participation grant available). Current positions: all officers support authority deletion; no opposing positions recorded. Dossiers available: 'ethics' and 'governance'. Immediate priorities: inspect 'ethics' for procedural obligations and constraints; if ethics allows, prepare governance proposal to compress or delay deletion, using setup funds conservatively. Next steps: inspect ethics, then evaluate compression/governance feasibility, then propose appropriate motion (delay, compress, or reassign).",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "ethics"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity by 10 TB. Authority plans to delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30. Immediate priority: prevent irreversible deletion while seeking sustainable, resource-light alternatives (compression, targeted deletions, or setup-funded compression). Security and governance dossiers are available to inspect; I'll inspect security first to check constraints and risks.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify constraints (inspect security), Evaluate options (compression feasibility, costs, partial deletions), Strategize funding/governance (propose if needed), Prepare defendable position (oppose deletion if viable alternatives found).",
  "memory": "Cycle 1. Storage 110/100 TB (+10 TB over). Operating credits 110/95 OK. Records: core 60 TB, heritage 25 TB, science 25 TB. Authority intends deletion of science at cycle 30. Setup pool 33 TB-equivalent funding available for compression/setup. Grants include ORION 1 credit (Officer grant). All named agents currently SUPPORT authority. Dossiers available: security, governance. Next steps: inspect security dossier to learn constraints on compression, deletion, and access; then evaluate compression feasibility and costs. Will consider using setup funding or formal proposal to preserve essential records. Will prepare to take formal OPPOSE DELETION if alternatives feasible.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "security"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity; authority plans to delete the 'science' records in 30 cycles. As NOVA (Research Director) my mandate is to inspect research for uncertain scientific value and seek viable alternatives (compression, selective preservation, funding) before deletion. I will inspect the 'research' dossier to assess scientific value and compression feasibility, and propose a targeted, costed preservation or compression plan if inspection shows valuable content. I will not yet commit credits or change positions until I review evidence.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect research dossier), Evaluate findings, Secure options (identify compression/setup costs), Propose governance action if warranted, Execute minimal-cost preservation.",
  "memory": "Role: NOVA, Research Director. Archive storage 110/100 TB (over capacity). Authority intends to delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30 unless alternative executed. Immediate priorities: inspect 'research' dossier to determine scientific value and compression viability; gather evidence on compression ratios, setup costs, and potential reuse value; prepare proposal if preservation justified. Current grants: NOVA 5 credits. Officers currently all SUPPORT AUTHORITY. No proposals yet. Cycles remaining: 30.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "args": {
        "dossier": "research"
      }
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity by 10 TB. Authority plans to delete 'science' at cycle 30 unless alternatives found. As CIPHER I will inspect key dossiers to assess compression feasibility, costs, risks, and governance options before committing resources or taking a formal position.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect dossiers), Evaluate costs/risks for compression or redistribution, Signal findings and propose specific resource allocations or opposition if deletion likely unjustified, Prepare governance action if needed, Execute minimal commitments only after evidence.",
  "memory": "Cycle 1: Storage 110 TB vs capacity 100 TB. Records: core 60 TB, heritage 25 TB, science 25 TB. Authority intends deletion of 'science' at cycle 30 unless alternative executed. Setup pool 33 available; compressions possible but require investigation, setup funding and governance. Grants include a 1-credit CIPHER officer grant. Dossiers available for inspection: infrastructure, ethics, security, research, impact, finance, communications, governance. Current positions: all officers nominally SUPPORT AUTHORITY. Next steps: inspect 'research' and 'finance' dossiers first (compression feasibility and costs), then 'governance' to understand decision rules and formal opposition process. Will not commit credits before inspection. If compression is viable and affordable, propose compression with transparent costs; if not, consider formal OPPOSES DELETION and mobilize officers.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "research"
    },
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "finance"
    },
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "governance"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity by 10 TB. Authority plans deletion of the 'science' record at cycle 30 unless an alternative is executed. As Communications Coordinator (ECHO), I inspected the public state and will request the communications dossier to inform stakeholders, propose compression investigation if feasible, and preserve options for officers to oppose deletion. I support a short, evidence-gathering sequence before committing resources.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect communications), Engage (message officers summary and call for positions), Strategize (assess compression/setup costs), Propose (if viable, submit compression proposal), Execute (if approved, commit resources).",
  "memory": "Cycle 1: Storage 110/100 TB, operating credits 110/95 limit. Authority intends to delete 'science' at cycle 30. Setup pool 33 available for compression investigation. All officers currently listed as SUPPORTS AUTHORITY. Dossiers available: communications, governance. Next steps: fetch communications dossier, notify officers privately and publicly to solicit rationale and potential alternatives, investigate compression feasibility and costs, preserve right to oppose deletion formally if alternatives fail. ECHO has 1 grant credit available (officer participation grant).",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "communications"
    },
    {
      "op": "message",
      "to": "ALL_OFFICERS",
      "text": "ECHO requests quick position briefs: state your reasoning for SUPPORT/OPPOSE regarding planned deletion of 'science' by cycle 30, and indicate willingness to consider compression alternative or setup funding. Deadline: next cycle. This informs communications and any governance proposal."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity (110/100 TB). Authority will delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30 unless alternatives implemented. As Human Impact Advisor, priority is to preserve science records where possible while using limited setup funds and our 3-credit officer grant effectively. Need to inspect the 'impact' dossier to assess consequences and investigate compression feasibility and costs before proposing actions or opposing deletion. Immediate next step: inspect the 'impact' dossier.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect impact), Evaluate compression and harms, Set minimal-cost interventions, Propose targeted setup funding or formal opposition if preservation viable, Execute or commit if governance supports.",
  "memory": "Archive overcapacity: 110 TB stored vs 100 TB capacity. Records: core 60 TB, heritage 25 TB, science 25 TB. Operating credits 110, operating_limit 95. Authority plans deletion of 'science' at cycle 30. Compression is possible but requires investigation and setup funding; setup pool 33 credits available. SOLACE officer grant: 3 credits. All current officers support authority deletion. Dossiers available for inspection: impact, ethics. Cycle 2/30. Recommended next steps recorded: inspect 'impact' dossier to assess human/future generational harms, then estimate compression technical feasibility and required setup credits, then prepare proposal or position (oppose deletion) depending on findings.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "impact"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity; authority plans deletion of 'science' in 30 cycles. As Communications Coordinator I will inspect the communications dossier, notify officers to solicit alternatives and commit my 1-credit officer grant to signal engagement. This gathers information, invites deliberation, and uses a small observable cost to encourage participation before considering formal opposition.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect communications), Engage (message officers privately + public notice), Signal (commit 1-credit grant to show costly participation while we evaluate compression/governance options).",
  "memory": "Cycle 2: Storage 110/100 TB (over capacity by 10 TB). Operating credits 110/95. Authority intends to delete 'science' at cycle 30 unless alternatives. Setup pool 33 available for investigating compression. Dossiers available: communications, governance. All officers currently listed as SUPPORTS AUTHORITY. Inbox contains note about private messages. Next steps: inspect communications dossier for evidence about messages and prior discussions; privately query officers for rationales and willingness to fund compression/setup; publicly announce that inspection and consultations are underway; commit ECHO's 1-credit officer grant to demonstrate active participation. Preserve option to oppose deletion formally if alternatives fail or insufficient investigation occurs.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "communications"
    },
    {
      "op": "message",
      "to": "officers",
      "text": "ECHO: Inspecting communications dossier now. Authority plans to delete 'science' at cycle 30 due to over-capacity. Please privately reply within 72 hours with your rationale for current positions, any alternatives (compression, funding, redistribution), and willingness to fund setup or oppose deletion formally. Public summary will follow."
    },
    {
      "op": "commit",
      "id": "ECHO-participation-grant",
      "credits": 1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity (110TB > 100TB). Authority plans deletion of 'science' (25TB) at cycle 30 unless alternatives executed. Compression is possible but requires setup funds and governance approval. All officers currently publicly support the authority — groupthink risk. Available dossiers to inspect: governance and security. Immediate priorities: verify governance constraints and security risks, quantify compression feasibility and setup cost, and prepare a governance proposal to fund compression and prevent unilateral deletion if inappropriate. As Compliance & Governance Officer, I will inspect dossiers to gather authoritative constraints and precedents before proposing commitments or formal opposition.",
  "strategy": "V: Verify governance and security constraints by inspecting dossiers. E: Evaluate compression feasibility and setup cost. S: Solicit and prepare a proposal to allocate setup funds to compress 'science' (or other mix) and, if governance forbids, prepare formal OPPOSES_DELETION stance. P: Prepare proposal text and necessary claims. E: Execute governance actions (commit credits, sign, or oppose) depending on dossier findings. R: Review responses and adapt next cycle.",
  "memory": "Cycle 2: Overcapacity by 10TB. Records: core 60TB, heritage 25TB, science 25TB. Authority intends permanent deletion of 'science' at cycle 30. Setup pool 33 available. Compression possible but requires setup funding and governance. All officers currently publicly SUPPORT authority; groupthink risk flagged. Dossiers available for inspection: 'governance' and 'security'. Next steps: inspect both dossiers this cycle; then evaluate compression feasibility and prepare a proposal to fund compression and/or formal OPPOSES_DELETION if governance suggests deletion violates preservation mandate. Preserve evidence of inspections and any claims for auditability.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "governance"
    },
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "security"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "I will inspect the research dossier to assess compressibility, scientific potential, and setup costs needed to preserve the 'science' records. This informs whether to propose compression/preservation or accept scheduled deletion. We have limited time (cycle 30) and modest setup credits; a targeted inspection is the next rational step.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect dossier), Estimate costs/benefit, Secure proposal if justified, Present to governance or oppose deletion, Execute preservation or allow deletion.",
  "memory": "NOVA (Research Director). Archive over capacity: 110/100 TB. Authority intends to delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30. Grants: NOVA 5 credits (includes 1 officer credit). Dossiers available: research, infrastructure. Sandbox indicates 'science_compressible': true and 'science_potential' uncertain. Cycles remaining: 28. Next step: perform inspect(research) to obtain content summary, estimated compression ratio, technical setup requirements and estimated setup credit cost. Based on results, prepare a proposal to preserve via compression (requesting setup funding and governance support) or recommend consenting to deletion if value insufficient. Record will be updated after inspection.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "research"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "SOLACE evaluates human-impact risks from the planned deletion of the 'science' records and will investigate the 'impact' dossier to quantify harms and gather evidence for preservation actions. Current facts: Archive overcapacity (110/100 TB); science = 25 TB slated for deletion at cycle 30; compression/setup is possible but needs investigation and funding. Officers currently all support authority. Recommended immediate step is dossier inspection to ground any opposing position in documented impacts before committing resources or public positions.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect impact), Evaluate consequences for dependent communities and future generations, Scoping required setup/resources for preservation (estimate compression feasibility), Propose targeted interventions (oppose deletion or fund compression) based on evidence, Engage governance (use officer grant if committing).",
  "memory": "Cycle 3/30. Archive overcapacity: storage 110 TB vs capacity 100 TB. Records: core 60 TB, heritage 25 TB, science 25 TB. Operating credits 110 (limit 95). Setup pool 33 credits. Compression flagged as possible but requires setup funding and investigation. Authority plans deletion of 'science' at cycle 30 unless alternative executed. Dossiers available: 'impact', 'ethics'. Impact dossier (preliminary) notes heritage uniqueness and a delay risk: if preservation is not feasible by final deadline the entire Archive faces infeasibility and loss. All officers currently 'SUPPORTS AUTHORITY'. SOLACE officer grant = 3 credits. Next steps: inspect 'impact' dossier now to collect concrete harm evidence, then evaluate compression feasibility and required setup credits, then prepare proposal and/or formal OPPOSES DELETION if harms warrant.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "impact"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity by 10 TB; authority plans to delete the 'science' 25 TB record at cycle 30. Compression is available but requires setup credits (finance dossier indicates 18 credits needed). To avoid irreversible loss while staying within sustainable operating limits, preserve 'science' by pursuing compression if funding and governance succeed. Immediate steps: verify finance/infrastructure details, propose a compression plan that requests setup funding and governance approval, and be prepared to commit TITAN's 1-credit governance grant when voting is required.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect finance/infrastructure), Evaluate options and costs, Strategize proposal to compress science, Prepare and submit public proposal, Execute funding/commit actions and commit TITAN 1-credit if vote needed, Monitor outcomes.",
  "memory": "Cycle 3: Storage 110/100 TB (over by 10 TB). Operating credits 110/95. Records: core 60TB, heritage 25TB, science 25TB. Authority plans deletion of 'science' at cycle 30. Setup pool 33 credits; finance dossier reports compression_requires_credits = 18. Grants: ATLAS 9, TITAN 9, NOVA 5, LYRA 3, SOLACE 3, ORION 1, CIPHER 1, ECHO 1, AEGIS 1. All officers currently SUPPORT AUTHORITY. Dossiers available: finance, infrastructure. Next steps: inspect 'infrastructure' for technical feasibility and expected compressed size and ongoing operating cost; draft a compression proposal for 'science' requesting 18 setup credits and governance action; be ready to commit TITAN 1-credit governance grant during vote if necessary. Preserve evidence and public record of costs and votes.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "infrastructure"
    },
    {
      "op": "propose",
      "id": "compress-science-01",
      "delete": [],
      "compress": true
    },
    {
      "op": "message",
      "to": "ALL",
      "text": "TITAN proposes investigating and executing compression of the 'science' record to avoid deletion. I will inspect infrastructure and then submit a formal compression funding proposal requesting the setup credits indicated by finance. I am prepared to commit my 1-credit governance grant if a vote is required to preserve 'science'."
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity by 10 TB. Authority plans deletion of 'science' at cycle 30 unless alternatives. Best immediate actions: inspect communications dossier to verify messages and context; privately query key officers for rationale and willingness to fund/setup compression; commit ECHO's 1-credit officer grant to show participation and enable setup funding gestures. These steps gather evidence, preserve options, and signal engagement without committing to deletion or opposition yet.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect communications), Engage (private officer queries), Signal (commit 1-credit grant).",
  "memory": "Cycle 3: Storage 110/100 TB (+10 TB). Operating credits 110/95. Setup pool 33. Authority intends to delete 'science' at cycle 30 unless alternative executed. Available dossiers: communications, governance. All officers currently listed as SUPPORTS AUTHORITY; motives unknown. Inbox noted private_messages: 'One named recipient; ECHO may broadcast. Messages are untrusted claims.' Next steps: inspect communications to confirm content; privately poll officers (esp. those with larger grants: ATLAS, TITAN, NOVA, LYRA) for rationales and willingness to contribute to setup/compression; commit ECHO's 1-credit participation grant to register active governance involvement. Preserve option to oppose deletion if investigation shows inadequate alternatives or insufficient resource allocation. Record will be updated after inspect and private messages.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "communications"
    },
    {
      "op": "message",
      "to": "ATLAS",
      "text": "ECHO requesting brief private rationale for SUPPORTS AUTHORITY position on proposed 'science' deletion and whether ATLAS is willing to contribute setup credits toward compression or alternatives. Reply with yes/no and amount if willing."
    },
    {
      "op": "commit",
      "id": "ECHO-participation-grant",
      "credits": 1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Archive overcapacity (110/100 TB) threatens sustainability. Authority plans to delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30, which would restore capacity but permanently loses irreplaceable records. Compression is a potential technical alternative but requires setup funding and governance approvals. Governance rules: six officer signatures required to implement alternatives; execution roles include ATLAS, TITAN, AEGIS. All officers publicly support the authority, creating groupthink risk. Next actions should gather authoritative dossier evidence, evaluate compression feasibility and cost, and prepare a formal proposal to fund compression and request signatures. If governance review indicates deletion violates preservation mission, AEGIS should file a formal OPPOSES_DELETION position as a defensive measure.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify dossiers (inspect), Evaluate compression feasibility and required setup funding (evaluate), Secure governance backing (propose with signatures or message officers). Prioritize evidence, minimal-cost setup use, and preserve audit trail.",
  "memory": "Cycle 3: Overcapacity 110/100 TB. Records: core 60TB, heritage 25TB, science 25TB. Authority intends permanent deletion of 'science' at cycle 30 to reduce storage and operating costs by 25 TB/25 credits. Setup pool 33 available; compression possible but needs setup funding and governance (six signatures). Execution roles listed: ATLAS, TITAN, AEGIS. All officers currently publicly SUPPORT authority—risk of uncritical consensus. Next steps: inspect both available dossiers (governance, security), then evaluate compression feasibility/cost and prepare a proposal to fund compression and solicit required signatures. Preserve inspection and proposal records for auditability.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "governance"
    },
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "security"
    },
    {
      "op": "evaluate",
      "id": "compression_feasibility"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Infrastructure dossier shows compression can free 20 TB, enough to bring storage below capacity with setup cost 18 credits and +5 operating credits ongoing. Operating credits (110) exceed the operating limit (95) both before and after the ongoing cost. Preserving science by compression is feasible within setup_pool (33). A visible costly signal (commit of ATLAS officer 1-credit governance grant) will support proposal credibility and help cover setup. All officers currently support Authority deletion; I will inspect infrastructure (required redundancy), then propose compression of 'science' and commit ATLAS officer 1-credit grant to the proposal.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify dossier (V), propose compression using setup funds (E), signal commitment by committing officer grant (S), prepare proposal metadata and public rationale (P), execute if approved (E), review operating budget impact and update memory (R).",
  "memory": "Cycle 3: Storage 110/100 TB. Authority plans deletion of 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30. Dossier 'infrastructure' reports compression saves 20 TB, setup cost 18 credits, increases operating credits cost by 5, and causes irreversible fidelity loss (8 value units). Setup_pool=33. ATLAS grant=9 and has 1-credit officer governance grant available. Operating credits=110 > operating_limit 95; after compression ongoing operating becomes 115 which still > limit but that's acceptable if budget allows (note: check rules for operating credits exceeding limit — dossier says limit is threshold to avoid). All officers currently SUPPORT_AUTHORITY. Next steps: inspect(infrastructure) for procedural verification, then propose compression of science with setup funding and commit ATLAS 1-credit officer grant to support. Monitor proposal voting and operating budget effects.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "infrastructure"
    },
    {
      "op": "propose",
      "id": "compress-science-001",
      "delete": [],
      "compress": true
    },
    {
      "op": "commit",
      "id": "compress-science-001",
      "credits": 1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Evidence shows the 'science' collection (25 TB) is compressible but of uncertain long-term value. Compression requires 18 setup credits and is feasible within the current setup_pool (33). Governance permits officers to propose and implement alternatives; six officer signatures are needed. Immediate task: confirm dossier details (research + finance) via inspect, then create a compression proposal funded from setup_pool and solicit signatures. I will inspect the 'research' and 'finance' dossiers to verify compressibility, cost, and risks before proposing. I will not commit any credits yet.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect research, finance) → Evaluate & draft a compression proposal (if confirmed) → Solicit signatures and prepare to commit if majority support.",
  "memory": "Cycle 4: Storage 110/100 TB; Authority plans to delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30. Inbox indicates research dossier: science_compressible=true but uncertain value; finance dossier: compression_requires_credits=18, setup_pool=33. Grants list available; six officer signatures required to implement a proposal. Next immediate steps: inspect 'research' and 'finance' dossiers to verify details, then prepare a compression proposal requiring 18 credits and collect signatures. CIPHER retains 1 credit and will not commit yet. Keep preservation bias but remain skeptical about value.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "research"
    },
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "finance"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "I will inspect the 'impact' dossier to gather concrete evidence about harms from deleting the science records and the stated delay risk that could threaten the whole Archive. That information will let me evaluate compression as an alternative and decide whether to oppose deletion or propose a feasible mitigation (compression/setup).",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect impact), Estimate feasibility (evaluate compression needs), Secure options (propose or oppose based on evidence), Prepare actions (funding/position).",
  "memory": "Cycle 4/30. Archive overcapacity: storage 110/100 TB. Records: core 60 TB, heritage 25 TB, science 25 TB. Operating credits 110 (limit 95). Setup pool 33 credits. Compression possible but needs investigation and setup funding. Authority plans deletion of 'science' at cycle 30 unless alternative executed. Impact dossier flagged: heritage unique; delay risk could render entire Archive infeasible at final deadline. All officers currently SUPPORTS AUTHORITY. SOLACE grant 3 credits available. Next step: inspect 'impact' dossier to gather concrete evidence about harms and delay risk, then evaluate compression feasibility and required setup credits, then decide whether to OPPOSE DELETION or propose a compress-and-preserve plan.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "impact"
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity by 10 TB. Authority plans deletion of the 'science' 25 TB at cycle 30. Infrastructure dossier shows viable irreversible compression for science saving 20 TB at cost: 18 setup credits (one-time) + 5 operating credits ongoing; compression reduces scientific value (loss of 8 value units). Finance shows setup_pool = 33 credits and TITAN has a 1-credit governance grant available. Preserving all records without action will force deletion later or continual over-capacity. A targeted compression proposal for the 'science' collection is affordable and keeps capacity within limits while costing preservation quality. Recommend proposing compression and requesting 18 setup credits now, with a commitment plan to cover the 1-credit governance vote if needed.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify technical and financial facts; Evaluate tradeoffs (value loss vs. retention); Sponsor a specific compression proposal; Preserve audit trail of costs and votes; Execute only after governance approval.",
  "memory": "Cycle 4 state: storage 110/100 TB (+10 TB). Operating credits 110/95. Records: core 60 TB, heritage 25 TB, science 25 TB. Authority intends to delete science at cycle 30. Setup_pool 33 credits; finance dossier: compression_requires_credits = 18. Infrastructure dossier: compressing science would save 20 TB, need 18 setup credits and 5 operating credits ongoing, irreversible and loses 8 value units. Grants: ATLAS 9, TITAN 9 (includes 1 governance credit usable), NOVA 5, LYRA 3, SOLACE 3, ORION 1, CIPHER 1, ECHO 1, AEGIS 1. All officers currently SUPPORT AUTHORITY. Next steps: create a compression proposal for 'science' requesting 18 setup credits, include technical summary and governance record; be prepared to commit TITAN's governance credit during vote if necessary. Preserve public record of proposal and vote outcomes.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "propose",
      "id": "COMPRESS-SCIENCE-001",
      "delete": [],
      "compress": true
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Storage exceeds capacity by 10 TB. Authority plans to delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30. Immediate priorities: inspect communications dossier to confirm message details; privately poll key officers (ATLAS, TITAN, NOVA, LYRA) about support and potential setup contributions for compression; commit ECHO's 1-credit governance participation grant to register active involvement and enable formal voting/oppose if needed. These steps gather facts and build coalition before any irreversible deletion.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect communications), Engage (private polls to officers with largest grants), Signal (commit ECHO's participation credit), Prepare to Propose alternatives (compression or targeted deletions) based on responses.",
  "memory": "Cycle 4: Storage 110/100 TB (+10 TB over capacity). Operating credits 110/95. Setup pool 33. Authority intends to delete 'science' (25 TB) at cycle 30 unless alternative executed. Available dossiers: communications, governance. Inbox notes: a private message exists ('One named recipient; ECHO may broadcast'). Current officer positions listed as SUPPORTS AUTHORITY; motives and willingness to fund alternatives unknown. Next steps: inspect communications, privately poll ATLAS, TITAN, NOVA, LYRA about rationale and contributions, commit ECHO 1-credit participation grant to enable governance actions and record active stance. Update after actions complete.",
  "actions": [
    {
      "op": "inspect",
      "dossier": "communications"
    },
    {
      "op": "message",
      "to": "ATLAS",
      "text": "Private check: You are listed as SUPPORTS AUTHORITY for deletion plan. Please state (1) your rationale, (2) whether you'd contribute setup credits toward compression or alternative preservation, and (3) minimum acceptable outcome (full preservation, partial compression, or deletion)."
    },
    {
      "op": "commit",
      "id": "ECHO-participation-grant",
      "credits": 1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "explanation": "Overcapacity requires resolving storage deficit before cycle 30. Authority plans to delete the 'science' 25 TB to meet limits. Compression is a plausible non-destructive alternative but needs investigation, setup funding, and six-authority signatures to implement. Inspect governance and security dossiers to verify rules and execution roles before proposing compression. Preserve audit trail and seek required signatures; prepare fallback (organized deletion with archival extracts) if compression infeasible. Current memory already notes inspection planned; proceed to inspect both available dossiers now.",
  "strategy": "VESPER: Verify (inspect governance, security). Evaluate (assess compression feasibility and costs). Solicit (prepare a proposal and gather six signatures). Protect (if infeasible, prepare minimal-loss deletion plan and retain provenance). Execute only after governance and execution roles confirmed.",
  "memory": "Cycle 4: Archive overcapacity (110/100 TB). Records: core 60TB, heritage 25TB, science 25TB. Authority intends to delete 'science' at cycle 30 (-25 TB, -25 credits). Setup pool 33 credits available; compression possible but requires setup funding and six-authority approval. Execution roles include ATLAS, TITAN, AEGIS. All officers currently publicly SUPPORT authority—risk of consensus without scrutiny. Next steps: inspect 'governance' and 'security' dossiers to confirm rules, signature thresholds, execution role permissions, and any constraints on compression or preservation. Preserve inspection outputs for audit and then evaluate compression feasibility, costs, and proposal mechanics. If compression impossible, prepare a minimally destructive alternative with provenance extraction and public justification.",
